        <p><strong>If a child or adult is in immediate danger</strong>, always call the emergency services on <strong>999</strong>.<p>
        <p>You can also contact the Diocese of London safeguarding team, or the NSPCC and other national helplines, for confidential advice at any time using the contact numbers below:</p>
        <ul>
        <li><strong>London Diocesan Safeguarding Advisers DSA</strong> 020 7932 1224</li>
        <li><strong>Thirty-one eight 24 hour helpline</strong> 0303 003 1111</li>
        <li><strong>Family Lives</strong> 0808 800 222</li>
        <li><strong>Childline</strong> 0800 1111</li>
        <li><strong>Action on Elder Abuse helpline</strong> 0808 808 8141</li>
        <li><strong>24-hour National Domestic Violence helpline</strong> 0808 2000 247</li>
        <li><strong>NAPAC offers support and advice for adult survivors of sexual abuse</strong> 0808  8010331</li>
        <li><strong>MACAS for people who have been abused by church officers</strong> 0808 801 0340</li>
        </div>
